tably\" in Q3. That is more than twice its C$450M Q2 2027 tender, so large deals can clear.\n- Norvane's 2027 spending is planned up 12%. It can likely fund that through debt, at a higher cost.\n- Pellham's 2027 spending is planned up 18%. It would have to lean harder on debt to replace its failed equity raise.\n- I found no leverage, ratings or total debt capacity data. I can't say how much more debt either utility can carry.\n\n**Equity**\n- Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering on 14 October because investor demand fell short.\n- Two utility share offerings were cut back in Q3. I found no detail on the second one.\n- Pellham is cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40%. It is resizing its Q1 2027 tender of about C$900M and deferring two substation programmes \"until financing improves\". So the capex plan is being cut to fit the financing.\n- I found no valuation data or Norvane equity targets. I'd treat a Pellham re-launch as a possibility, not an expectation.\n\n**What it means for VLTX:** Pellham's tender will probably come in well below C$900M. VLTX won 60% of the last tender round. I didn't check how much of VLTX's orders come from Pellham.\n\n**What to watch:** Q4 spreads and any Pellham bond deal.\n\nSources: n5.r1 (debt) and n6.r1 (equity).","ttft_ms":1437,"type":"result","duration_ms":43710,"uuid":"4357e90f-81fe-470f-9ae8-6b206d209898","ttft_stream_ms":987,"time_to_request_ms":268,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":30,"system_prompt":15,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":23,"input_hooks":5,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":19,"tool_pool_refresh":13,"init_message":65,"init_frame_send":10,"engine_pickup":5,"loop_entry":8,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":7,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":24,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":5,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":21,"request_build":8},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":155,"ti